HPX 1.9.1: retain observable 128-bit operations in the atomic link probe.

Optimized Clang can eliminate all operations on the unused local atomic in the
original probe. The test then succeeds without libatomic, although HPX's deque
requires __atomic_load_16 and __atomic_compare_exchange_16. Use an externally
visible atomic and test compare-exchange as well as load/store so HPX's existing
CMake fallback detects and propagates libatomic only when it is needed. Match
the 16-byte alignment of HPX's tagged pointer pairs.

This is a local compatibility fix for the observed ROCm 6.4.1 HPX link failure;
it changes detection only, not HPX's runtime algorithms or Kokkos sources.

diff --git a/cmake/tests/cxx11_std_atomic_128bit.cpp b/cmake/tests/cxx11_std_atomic_128bit.cpp
--- a/cmake/tests/cxx11_std_atomic_128bit.cpp
+++ b/cmake/tests/cxx11_std_atomic_128bit.cpp
@@ -10,21 +10,23 @@
 #include <cstdint>
 
 template <typename T>
-void test_atomic()
+void test_atomic(std::atomic<T>& a)
 {
-    std::atomic<T> a;
     a.store(T{});
     T i = a.load();
-    (void)i;
+    (void) a.compare_exchange_strong(i, T{});
 }
 
-struct uint128_type
+struct alignas(16) uint128_type
 {
     std::uint64_t left;
     std::uint64_t right;
 };
 
+// Keep the atomic operations observable even with compiler optimization.
+std::atomic<uint128_type> a;
+
 int main()
 {
-    test_atomic<uint128_type>();
+    test_atomic(a);
 }
